and associated files distributed under this license.

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Software, in whole or in
part, that is intended for, directed toward, or that in practice
results in commercial advantage, monetary compensation, or other
consideration of value, for you or for any third party, whether the
benefit is direct or indirect and whether or not money changes
hands. Commercial Use includes, without limitation:
  (a) selling, licensing, sublicensing, leasing, or renting the
      Software, in original or modified form;
  (b) using the Software to provide, support, or operate a paid
      product, subscription, or service, including a hosted,
      remote, or network-accessible service, even if the Software
      itself is never distributed, sold, or exposed to end users;
  (c) incorporating the Software, in whole or in part, into a
      product, firmware image, device, or service that is sold,
      licensed, leased, or otherwise monetized;
  (d) using the Software in the internal operations, research and
      development, testing, or infrastructure of a for-profit
      entity, where such use provides any commercial benefit to
      that entity, regardless of whether the Software or any
      product built with it is ever sold or released externally;
  (e) using the Software to perform paid consulting, contracting,
      freelance, or agency work for a client, or to fulfill any
      paid engagement, deliverable, or statement of work;
  (f) using the Software to create, deliver, or support paid
      training, courses, tutorials, certifications, workshops, or
      similar educational offerings for which any fee is charged;
  (g) using the Software to generate, mine, farm, or otherwise
      produce cryptocurrency, tokens, or other assets of tradeable
      or monetary value;
  (h) using the Software to develop, demonstrate, or support a
      product, prototype, or pitch for the purpose of raising
      investment, securing funding, or otherwise attracting
      financial backing;
  (i) monetizing the Software, a derivative of it, or content
      relating to it through advertising, sponsorships,
      affiliate links, paywalls, donations tied to service access,
      or similar revenue mechanisms; or
  (j) using the Software in connection with research or
      development that is funded by a commercial sponsor, grant,
      or contract where the resulting work product, findings, or
      IP are intended for commercial exploitation.

"Private Use" means personal, educational, research, or
non-commercial hobbyist use by an individual or non-profit entity
that does not fall within any of the categories described above.
For the avoidance of doubt, Private Use includes: purely personal
experimentation and learning; coursework and research at academic
institutions that is not funded or directed toward commercial
exploitation as described in (j); and publishing or sharing your
own unmodified or modified copies of the Software at no charge,
where you receive no commercial benefit, direct or indirect, from
doing so. If you are uncertain whether a particular use qualifies
as Private Use, contact the copyright holder before proceeding.

"Contributor" means the copyright holder and any individual or
entity that has contributed code, documentation, or other material
to the Software with the copyright holder's acceptance.

